WEBVTT

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.080
Gundam 0080 is next.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:11.410
Hmm.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.700
I don't get it.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:15.780
I know that.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.460
What I just don't understand is why you think this plan can work, you know?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.480
Honestly, I'm not much of a planner.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.140
Though I like to make schedules and to-do lists,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.640
I've never done things according to the schedule even once in my life.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.960
- Once I call out to him, all I can do is wait.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.860
That's about all I can hope for right now.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.580
- Sit there and wait?

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.220
- Is that bad?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.600
- That doesn't seem any different

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.600
from just doing nothing.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.990
- I think it would be good enough for him

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:48.100
if I can get a message through saying that I'm waiting.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.100
I think the rest is up to Tsukasa from there.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.900
At that point, what choice do I have

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:58.960
except to wait for him, right?

00:00:58.960 --> 00:00:59.760
- What is it?

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.960
I hope that feeling of yours gets across to him.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.030
BT, are you scheming again?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.860
Not just yet.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.910
Say what?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.440
Just kidding.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.250
It'll be tough for you to just sit and wait.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.570
Speaking from experience?

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.080
Perhaps.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
You're the one that told me to meet Mimi Roo in the very beginning.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.910
Why now?

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:10.930
I wanna go.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:22.140
That's...it?

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.700
That's all I could come up with, me and my feeble intellect.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.700
Hey now, I don't like the way you said that.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.000
Huh?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.020
"You don't give yourself much credit, Mimiru. You're really a bright girl."

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.270
"No, sir. I'm just a moron."

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:41.320
"Even when the Crimson Knights were all out looking for him, they couldn't find him.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:46.720
Perhaps Tsukasa has a special place, a secluded place that only he can escape to."

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.720
"He is a character that surpassed the system. It wouldn't be strange for him to have such a place."

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:57.220
"If that's the case, it'll be impossible to search for Tsukasa and we won't be able to find him now."

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.000
"Mimiru's plan may be right. Perhaps the

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
The best and only choice we really have on the net is to wait.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.170
Well, I don't think it's best, but it may very well be the only...

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.600
What about outside?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.140
Well, there were... a lot of things going on.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.140
How convenient!

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.090
You're retorting in unison?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.070
So, in other words, you really haven't found anything too important.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.070
You get lines by connecting points together.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:26.090
When the lines close, the outlines for the situation start to appear.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.000
The more points there are to connect, the more the outline becomes apparent.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.990
But right now, we're still looking for those points to connect.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.010
I'll leave this stuff outside to you, Bear. I'll just sit here and wait it out.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.450
Wait. On second thought, maybe I'll go make myself some tea.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:49.440
Okay. Hmm?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.440
When a player steps away from their terminal, this is what happens to them.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.480
It's something that's so obvious.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.000
However, Tsukasa doesn't seem to lose the control of his character, despite nothing.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.550
not being in front of a terminal as we know.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.740
- Yeah, I'm sure the reason for that

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.960
can't be discovered from the outside.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.160
I have a feeling that the key to solving this mystery

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.520
lies within this game.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.310
Of course, that would be connected to Tsukasa as well.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.010
However, if we get close to discovering the core

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.030
of the matter, it may be a little too much for Mimibru.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.990
At least, that's kind of what this old man is thinking.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.810
- So, you want me to seek that information?

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.640
- You may need to do a little bit of research

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.000
in a different direction from our

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Mr. Bear is good at using people.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Please don't address me like that.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.330
Depending upon how we carry this out,

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.190
Sora may also be of use.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.050
I'm not so sure.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:49.540
Have you seen little Tsukasa anywhere?

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.200
We don't know about him.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.960
I see.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.060
Mm-hmm.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.440
Excuse me.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.600
Do you know about little Tsukasa?

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.490
Wait a minute!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:15.080
You have to answer the question properly.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.500
I know of him.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.890
Hmm, good. Where did you see him?

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.090
The message boards.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.530
You're dumb and worthless.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.100
You're right. This situation is a problem.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.410
However, the thought of using the knights to come down and control Sora's actions...

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.870
Lady Subaru, though it was just a short time, that player once acted in conjunction with the Crimson Knights.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:52.540
If we allow such a man to wreak havoc unchecked, the pride of the knights...

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.140
Pride is at stake. I see. Is there anything else?

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.000
There's the matter.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.670
of those monsters it looks like that is starting to calm down at this rate we

