00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.000
Sorry, I'm waiting for someone.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.700
Hey, didn't you say that before?

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.740
Huh? You don't say.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.880
Yeah, you sure did. I remember you giving me that line.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.310
Huh, maybe you were just sitting here waiting for that guy Godot.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.510
Huh?

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:15.140
Oh, well. That wasn't very funny at all.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.950
Huh. See you around.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.850
Huh. Oh, there you are.

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:21.070
Of course here I am.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:24.100
So, you haven't slept a wink?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.950
I feel like I wouldn't be waiting if I fell asleep.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.670
I understand that. But you gotta get some rest.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.840
- I can take your place for an hour or so.

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.320
At least some sleep will do you good.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.780
- If I'm not here when he comes,

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.800
I'm sure he'll go into hiding again somewhere.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.140
I don't want that to happen.

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:41.500
- Think you can last until he gets here?

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.800
- I'm still young.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.260
I'll do my best during this short vacation.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.660
- Your will is impressive.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.420
- Hey, what do you know about Godot?

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.960
- Did B.T. mention that?

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.780
- No, a passerby mentioned it to me.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.120
What is Godot, anyway?

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.000
- He's talking about a famous play.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.700
You mean, like, theater?

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.950
What's it about?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:06.120
Two men wait and wait for a man named Godot to arrive.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.130
That's all there is to the play, I'm afraid.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.360
Godot never shows up, does he?

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.320
That's right.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.350
I'm sure Tsukasa will be here.

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:17.330
I'm waiting, because I know he'll come.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:24.050
I'm not a kid anymore!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.670
Oh, pardon me.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.750
So you're the one called BT?

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:34.990
Yeah, what about it?

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.450
I have nothing against you.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.150
This is the type of guy I'm role-playing,

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:39.450
so don't worry about it.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.760
In any event, do you want me to call you BT?

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:45.780
I hate to tell you, but you're not that popular these days.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.900
Well, I hate what you would call fads.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.680
And no matter what anyone says, I personally

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.250
like this character.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.010
So, do you have any pet peeves?

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:53.910
Plenty.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.810
Would you like to hear about some of them?

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.530
I'll decline for now.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:00.000
Now let's see, didn't Subaru arrange

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.530
for this place just so we could talk about such things uninterrupted?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.070
So let's get to the point.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.550
What is it you want?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.610
To discuss Tsukasa and things concerning him

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:13.810
and something that might be a threat to the future balance of the world.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:17.540
Those conversations, just my style.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.800
know you're there, so it's a waste of time

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:43.720
for you to hide. Or

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.100
do you want me to come

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:46.120
down?

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:55.940
Mm-hmm. Come have a

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.100
seat. Let's talk. There's nothing

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.000
to talk about. Are you wondering

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:07.030
How I knew you were here this very spot BT wrong you're a popular topic on the

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:11.300
message boards they're saying there's a female heavy blade just sitting and

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:18.160
waiting for someone sound familiar you see you see it's harder for Tsukasa to

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:23.740
come out here isn't it but you just had to meet him out here that's cuz we used

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:28.820
to come here and that's it I can't believe how easy you made this there are

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.000
plenty of places where you

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.900
You could go unnoticed like some dungeon out there, but no.

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.840
Um, yeah.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:40.350
Well, I don't mind, because I can wait for Tsukasa here with you.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.300
You're gonna wait, too?

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:44.300
I have the right to wait, don't I?

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:47.300
I was the one who let him escape from the Crimson Knights.

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:51.200
You ruined my chance to get him because you turned out to be utterly useless.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.110
You remember that, don't you?

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:57.820
I now know what's been on Subaru's mind.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:00.000
I also know now that a wave master named Tsukasa

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:01.570
Casa is the focal point of it all.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.730
Am I on the right track?

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.070
But to truly get to the bottom of this,

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.150
the knights, starting with Silver Knight, are of no use.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.250
I have no wish to start a coup d'etat.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.630
And I'm not one for political warfare, either.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.070
What else is there to do?

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.110
What can we do by ourselves without a group to fall back on?

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:21.010
Hmm, well, there are advantages to being just the two of us.

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:21.490
BT.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:22.580
Hmm?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.040
I've never been one to beat around the bush.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.280
So tell me the main point straight up.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.020
You act and I analyze.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.000
If we combine it,

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.460
our skills we can gather information more quickly than the others and most importantly we can do so

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:41.300
without being noticed. Information? Tsukasa is just one of the processes that is currently making

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:46.280
itself visible. The cause is something else entirely. Unless we figure out what that something

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:51.630
else is there will be chaos. That's the reason why Subaru is interested in its origin as well.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:57.350
Do you have any leads? Tsukasa is an anomaly because his actions surpass that of the system.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.000
He operates outside the normal rule

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.440
of the world. We know that there is an item out there that surpasses the system as well.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:10.680
That can't be. Such a thing doesn't exist the way you say it does.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:12.730
Can you really say that for sure?

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:16.910
I once looked for an item like the one that you mentioned, but it didn't exist anywhere

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:17.830
in the world.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:24.770
Well, everything about the world doesn't need to be visible to our eyes. There is no

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:28.740
need to deny the existence of something just because you couldn't find it.

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.960
If you feel up to it, let me know.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:46.000
Oh, to find the key of the twilight, huh?

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.650
This is an omen.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.420
Okay, what are you gonna do, Grimp?

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:59.590
What time?

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.520
What?

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:02.820
Didn't you set a time?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:03.540
Nope.

